I added exact prices for the six xAI (Grok) models that /cost was misbilling. Mistral had nothing to fix: it had no mismatched rows when I started. Build, test, clippy and fmt all pass, and the work is committed as fc12df10 with a comment posted on #1012.

The problem. These six models were billed at a generic Grok 4 guess of $3 input / $15 output per million tokens, with cached-input reads counted as free. That read 2.4–6× high on output.

The fix. Each model now has its own price, taken from xAI's own models page (fetched today) and checked against models.dev (the price catalogue the audit compares against). Prices are per million tokens, in the order input / cached-input read / output:

| Model | Price |
|---|---|
| grok-4.3, grok-4.20-0309-reasoning, -non-reasoning, grok-4.20-multi-agent-0309 | 1.25 / 0.20 / 2.50 |
| grok-4.5 | 2.00 / 0.30 / 6.00 |
| grok-4.6 | 2.20 / 0.55 / 6.60 |

• `grok-4.6` costs 10% more in one region. xAI charges 2.00 / 0.50 / 6.00 in us-east-1 and us-west-2, and 10% more in us-central-1. yoyo can't tell which region served a request, so I used the higher price, as the docs' rule says (estimates should read high, not low). That means grok-4.6 still shows as a mismatch against models.dev. It's a deliberate one, like gemini-3.6-flash.
• Long prompts. xAI doubles every price above 200,000 prompt tokens. That's now modelled the same way as Gemini 3.1 Pro: the per-turn breakdown in /cost applies it, but the session total still uses the base price.

Audit result (the price-check test run with --ignored):
• Before: matched 65, mismatched 36.
• After: matched 70, mismatched 31.

I added 6 prices and the mismatch count fell by 5; the one left is grok-4.6 by choice. Nothing new started mismatching.

Tests. Two new tests in price_audit_tests.rs failed before the change and pass after:
• One checks the price table against xAI's page. It also checks that near-miss ids keep their old prices: grok-4, the aliases and grok-4-mini.
• The other checks the long-prompt rule: higher prices above 200K, normal prices at exactly 200K, and none for the generic grok-4 guess.

Still open (also on #1012):
• `grok-4.7` is priced too low for some users. Its price comes from the yoagent library, which uses the lower regional rate. That breaks the read-high rule for anyone on us-central-1. The docs now list it as the third place where estimates read low. The fix is either a yoyo-side price for it or a request to yoagent; I haven't done either.
• xAI's alias names (grok-4.3-latest, grok-4.20-reasoning, …) aren't listed on models.dev, so I couldn't check them against two sources. They keep the $3 / $15 guess.
• Remaining mismatches by provider: OpenAI 16, Google 8, Z.ai 5, DeepSeek 1, xAI 1 (grok-4.6, deliberate). None of these models appear in yoyo's own model lists; they're only reachable by typing --model <id>.

src/format/cost.rs is now 3,623 lines. That's over its recorded limit of 3,605 but within the 50-line allowance.
